      "decisions": [
        "Force RLS on subject_scopes and subject_principal_bindings with a catalog-only, fixed-search-path policy helper and closed role grants.",
        "Permit authority-metadata reads only for validated internal command owners and auditors; a subject principal with any authority ACL, ownership, or role-graph drift sees no rows.",
        "Retain SECURITY INVOKER row and statement triggers as the independent metadata write boundary, including TRUNCATE denial.",
        "Require the exact externally provisioned kl_trusted_admin_login with one inherited, non-SET, non-admin trusted-admin membership and no extra reachable roles for registration.",
        "Treat inbound foreign keys to S38, S42, S45, S46, and S47 as a closed inventory of eight canonical, subject-keyed constraints checked before upgrade and during registration, lookup, and RLS.",
        "Install one canonical superuser-owned ddl_command_start event trigger during external two-phase cluster bootstrap and require its exact enabled function inventory before d4 upgrade or downgrade.",
        "Bind DDL denial to authenticated session_user and the canonical subject-login name pattern, so deleting or corrupting a binding cannot enable SET ROLE DDL.",
        "Run protected row triggers as SECURITY INVOKER and pass invoking current_user to fixed-search-path SECURITY DEFINER helpers for exact command-owner, binding, subject, namespace, role-graph, ACL, ownership, and foreign-key validation.",
        "Force RLS on S38, S42, S45, S46, and S47 and retain INSERT, UPDATE, DELETE, and TRUNCATE trigger enforcement so BYPASSRLS never becomes a direct bound-subject write path.",
        "Acquire registration ACCESS SHARE and downgrade ACCESS EXCLUSIVE locks in the global order S38, S42, S45, S46, S47, subject scopes, principal bindings; hold downgrade locks through destructive DDL.",
        "Preserve frozen S51-before-S01 and T6/T7 command-owner semantics; the RLS, DML, DDL, metadata, and inbound-FK guards enforce persistence boundaries only."
      ],
      "known_limitations": [
        "Cluster roles, subject credentials, memberships, ownership handoff, continuous role audit, and canonical superuser event-trigger installation remain external two-phase deployment responsibilities documented in docs/contracts/subject_scope.md.",
        "Subject principals must never receive SUPERUSER or BYPASSRLS. PostgreSQL cannot mediate SELECT after a cluster administrator grants either attribute; ALTER ROLE, event-trigger administration, and direct superuser data access remain trusted cluster-administration boundaries.",
        "Operators must retire all classifications, bindings, and protected S38/S42/S45/S46/S47 data before downgrade.",
        "No product requirement PASS or production auto-activation is claimed."
      ],
      "follow_up_tasks": [
        "Run fresh SHA-bound GENERAL, PROTOCOL, DB_CONCURRENCY, and SECURITY_DATA_BOUNDARY independent reviews on the final reviewable head."
      ],
