      "summary": "Added a reusable pure Authorization validity/executability evaluator and wired it into the existing T6 and T7 repository owners. T6 now persists one deterministic finite certificate whose end is the exact minimum of requested, manifest, resolution, admission-freshness, validation, projection, transitive artifact, policy TTL, request deadline and calendar bounds, using each persisted dependency's authoritative start and canonical UTC timestamp representation; missing, future-effective, or invalid basis denies atomically, and approved TIMELESS artifacts contribute no artificial end. T7 rereads exact subject, content, scope, epoch, targeted S43, applicable S18/S17, policy, session/head, dependency and database-time facts under the existing S51-to-S01 gate, returning only a non-bearer current observation. Isolated PostgreSQL interleavings prove committed transitive revocation is seen after lock wait while unrelated revocation does not deny. The TEST-subject E2E uses canonical trusted-admin registration, an isolated policy/environment and TEST_ONLY scope, and stops without writing an execution binding.",
