      "decisions": [
        "Preserve all lifecycle bytes except readiness_lifecycle_candidate(before); retain original SQL/authentication/credentials/image/ports/volume/namespace semantics.",
        "Create only the byte-exact ratified additive kl074-readiness workflow; both existing workflows remain byte-identical.",
        "Use only dedicated GitHub-hosted local Docker for actual-image coldstarts and full legacy DB suites; no developer/shared Docker execution.",
        "Replace coarse socket sampling after its measured-witness failure with a bounded concurrent read-only observer; lifecycle TCP/SQL is not delayed by that observer.",
        "Verify run/job/head/attempt/repository identities and downloaded archive digest before recording PASS; preserve all raw artifact bytes and historical failure diagnostics in envelopes.",
        "Keep product requirements and release gates separate; no product/release/auto-activation PASS is claimed."
      ],
      "known_limitations": [
        "The first hosted candidate failed because coarse observations missed the short socket-only window; its full-suite step was NOT_RUN. Its verified raw failure artifact is retained separately and never counted as PASS.",
        "Evidence pins the actual configured PostgreSQL image and entrypoint observed at tested_commit; no inference-only or production claim is made.",
        "The draft evidence-collection heads correctly failed the missing-result merge gate. Fresh independent reviews, the review-record-only suffix check and every applicable final-head CI/gate must pass before normal merge."
      ],
      "follow_up_tasks": [
        "Complete fresh SHA-bound GENERAL, DB_CONCURRENCY and SECURITY_DATA_BOUNDARY reviews; persist only task-scoped review records afterward.",
        "Verify final relevant-head normal CI, hosted readiness evidence job and selected merge gate before normal merge.",
        "Record post-merge integration separately without modifying this reviewed result."
      ],
